.\"
.TH "HTMLINPUTELEMENT.SELECT_EVENT" "3JS" "October 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLInputElement.select_event \- HTMLInputElement: select event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]select\f[B]\f[R] event of the \f[CR]HTMLInputElement\f[R]
interface fires when the selection\(cqs extent or direction is changed
programmatically, or when the user selects text.
.PP
This event is not fired when nothing is selected and the caret is moved
by the user.
Only the \f[CR]selectionchange\f[R] event fires in this case.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqselect\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onselect = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A generic \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Selection logger
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]input\f[R] value=\(dqTry selecting some text in this element.\(dq />
<\f[B]p\f[R] id=\(dqlog\(dq></\f[B]p\f[R]>
.EE
.IP
.EX
\f[B]function\f[R] logSelection(event) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] log = document.getElementById(\(dqlog\(dq);
  \f[B]const\f[R] selection = event.target.value.substring(
    event.target.selectionStart,
    event.target.selectionEnd,
  );
  log.textContent = \(gaYou selected: ${selection}\(ga;
}

\f[B]const\f[R] input = document.querySelector(\(dqinput\(dq);
input.addEventListener(\(dqselect\(dq, logSelection);
.EE
.SS Using the \f[CR]onselect\f[R] event handler property
You can also set up the event handler using the \f[CR]onselect\f[R]
property (but note that this replaces other event listeners added using
\f[CR]onselect\f[R], if any):
.IP
.EX
input.onselect = logSelection;
.EE
